WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.312
Welcome to Module 12, Views and Reusable S Q L Objects in Postgres.

00:00:06.312 --> 00:00:14.362
In Module 11, you learned how to organize advanced queries with common table expressions and window functions.

00:00:14.362 --> 00:00:18.547
Those tools are useful inside one analysis.

00:00:18.547 --> 00:00:26.478
But what happens when the same trusted logic is needed by many reports, many analysts, or many applications?

00:00:26.928 --> 00:00:29.355
That is where this module begins.

00:00:29.355 --> 00:00:35.790
We are moving from writing one good query to creating reusable database interfaces.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.375
We will start with standard views.

00:00:38.375 --> 00:00:44.235
Then we will look at materialized views, which store a snapshot of a query result.

00:00:44.235 --> 00:00:52.100
We will also discuss dependencies, updates through views, access boundaries, and freshness.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:58.895
The main question to keep in mind is simple: which logic should stay inside one query,

00:00:58.895 --> 00:01:03.525
and which logic is stable enough to become a reusable database object?
